span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> N <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> get<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1276\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T,N<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> a <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (4) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx14\">(constexpr since C++14)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Extracts the <code>I</code><sup>th</sup> element from the array using <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/tuple/tuple-like\">tuple-like</a> interface.\n</p><p><code>I</code> must be an integer value in range <span><code>[</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span><code>,&nbsp;</code><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">N</span><code>)</code></span>. This is enforced at compile time as opposed to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array/at\">at()</a></span> or <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array/operator_at\">operator[]</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> a\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> array whose contents to extract\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A reference to the <code>I</code><sup>th</sup> element of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;array&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1276\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a> v<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\nstatic_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>get<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> get<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> get<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1276\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> a<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// set values:</span>\n    get<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, get<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span